<mxCell id="gh_box" value="" style="rounded=1;arcSize=2;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;strokeColor=#EF6C00;fillColor=#F6F8FA;fontColor=#EF6C00;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=4;spacingBottom=6;dashed=1;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2300" y="1850" width="600" height="140" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="legend_l" value="&lt;b style=&#x27;font-size:14px&#x27;&gt;Flows (1/2)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#1565C0&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;1&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;DNS lookup of eventide.creasy.club (Cloudflare delegates the name to Route 53, which answers with the ALB)&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#1565C0&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;2&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;HTTPS request, in through the internet gateway — the WAF inspects it, TLS ends at the ALB with the ACM certificate&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#1565C0&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;3&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;ALB → ingress-nginx NodePort (the ALB is built by Terraform, not by Kubernetes)&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#1565C0&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;4&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;ingress routes by path: / → web · /api/events · /api/regis (+WebSocket) · /api/auth · /api/payment&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#2E7D32&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;5&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;/files/* is rewritten by the ingress to S3 through the gateway endpoint; only public/* is readable&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#455A64&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;6&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;event, registration, payment ask auth to validate the session cookie (get-session, cached in Redis 60 s)&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#2E7D32&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;7&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;auth, event, registration, payment → RDS Proxy → RDS (one database, one role, pool of 4 per pod)&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#2E7D32&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;8&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;same four → ElastiCache over TLS with an AUTH token (session cache, event cache, live-seat pub/sub)&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#2E7D32&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;9&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;S3 reads/writes (avatar, cover, gallery) from either tier use the S3 gateway endpoint&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#C2185B&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;10&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;same four enqueue mail (template + props) on SQS, through the sqs interface endpoint&lt;br&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=2;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=12;fontStyle=0;strokeColor=#9E9E9E;fillColor=#FAFAFA;fontColor=#232F3E;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=4;spacingBottom=6;dashed=0;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="250" y="2040" width="1620" height="250" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="legend_r" value="&lt;b style=&#x27;font-size:14px&#x27;&gt;Flows (2/2)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#C2185B&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;11&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;mail-worker long-polls, renders the React Email template, deletes; 5 failed receives → DLQ&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#EF6C00&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;12&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;mail-worker → NAT → internet gateway → Gmail SMTP (dry-run log when no App Password)&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#EF6C00&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;13&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;payment → NAT → Stripe (checkout, verify, refund)&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#EF6C00&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;14&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Stripe → webhook, over the public https site (the endpoint registered in Stripe)&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#EF6C00&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;15&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;auth → NAT → Google (sign-in)&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#455A64&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;16&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;web asks event for the page&#x27;s title / image (Open Graph head)&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#6A1B9A&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;17&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;make up/down = terraform apply, state in S3 (permanent: VPC, ECR, S3, SQS, secrets, DNS · nightly: EKS, NAT, endpoints, RDS, Proxy, Redis, ALB, WAF, alarms)&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#6A1B9A&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;18&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;push to main: build + push images (a), helm upgrade + kubectl + db-migrate (b), read secrets (c)&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#6A1B9A&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;19&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;kubelet pulls images from ECR through the ecr.api / ecr.dkr endpoints; ingress-nginx and metrics-server come from the ECR mirrors&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#6A1B9A&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;20&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;15 CloudWatch alarms (ALB 5xx / health / latency, RDS, Proxy pinning, Redis, DLQ, node CPU, WAF burst) → SNS; dashboard eventide&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Colours&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#1565C0&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;━ user request&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt; · &lt;font color=&#x27;#455A64&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;━ service call&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt; · &lt;font color=&#x27;#2E7D32&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;━ data store&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt; · &lt;font color=&#x27;#C2185B&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;━ mail (SQS)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt; · &lt;font color=&#x27;#EF6C00&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;━ external API&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&#x27;#6A1B9A&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;┅ deploy / control&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt; · &lt;font color=&#x27;#757575&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;┅ DNS / certificate / WAF setup&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt; · &lt;font color=&#x27;#EF6C00&#x27;&gt;&lt;b&gt;▭ orange dashed box = not live yet&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=2;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=12;fontStyle=0;strokeColor=#9E9E9E;fillColor=#FAFAFA;fontColor=#232F3E;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=4;spacingBottom=6;dashed=0;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1890" y="2040" width="1260" height="250" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="notes" value="&lt;b style=&#x27;font-size:14px&#x27;&gt;Differences from the target architecture (AWS_Diagram_Tool.jpg)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;CloudFront → ALB + WAF&lt;/b&gt; (CloudFront is denied in the Learner Lab; the WAF is not in the target) · &lt;b&gt;NLB → ALB&lt;/b&gt; · &lt;b&gt;Shield&lt;/b&gt;: only the automatic Shield Standard (Advanced is denied) · &lt;b&gt;not production-grade, by lab constraint&lt;/b&gt;: single AZ, no RDS backups (the database is rebuilt every session), pods use the 4-hour session credentials (no IRSA), EKS API public, WAF and ALB logging off, platform up only during sessions (the $50 cap)." style="rounded=1;arcSize=2;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=12;fontStyle=0;strokeColor=#EF6C00;fillColor=#FFF8E1;fontColor=#232F3E;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=4;spacingBottom=6;dashed=1;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="250" y="2300" width="2900" height="100" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="title" value="&lt;b style=&#x27;font-size:26px&#x27;&gt;Eventide — AWS infrastructure, as built (production layout)&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=26;fontColor=#232F3E;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="14" width="1800" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="subtitle" value="AWS Academy Learner Lab · us-east-1 · dedicated VPC 10.20.0.0/16, single-AZ (1a; 1b holds only the subnets ALB / EKS / RDS require) · arrows point from the caller to the callee · live at &lt;b&gt;https://eventide.creasy.club&lt;/b&gt; · differences from the target &lt;code&gt;AWS_Diagram_Tool.jpg&lt;/code&gt; are listed at the bottom" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=13;fontColor=#555555;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="52" width="3300" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
